  "summary": "Yūrei-zu (幽霊図) are a genre of Japanese art consisting of painted or woodblock print images of ghosts, demons and other supernatural beings.",
  "description": "Yūrei-zu (幽霊図) are a genre of Japanese art consisting of painted or woodblock print images of ghosts, demons and other supernatural beings. They are considered to be a subgenre of fūzokuga, \"pictures of manners and customs\". These types of art works reached the peak of their popularity in Japan in the mid- to late 19th century.",
